+## Fuel check
+
+Below the table — once an aircraft is set — a **Fuel check** block weighs the route against the
+tanks:
+
+- **Trip** — the Total fuel above (leg burn plus the taxi/take-off allowance).
+- **Reserve** — a VFR reserve held back, shown as gallons at the cruise burn. Its minutes are the
+  aircraft's **Reserve (min)** figure (45 min by default); the label says which, e.g. *Reserve
+  (45 min)*.
+- **Alternate (gal)** — an optional figure you type for a diversion. It is kept with the filing
+  profile (`navaid.fpl.altGal`, Drive-synced).
+- **Total required** — Trip + Reserve + Alternate.
+- **Remaining** — usable fuel minus the total required. It turns **red** when it goes negative.
+- **Endurance** — how long the tanks last at the cruise burn (`usable ÷ Gal/h`), as `H:MM`.
+
+When the total required is more than the usable fuel holds, the block shows a red **“Over tanks by
+N gal”** warning — spelt out, not colour alone. Set the aircraft's **usable fuel** for the tank
+comparison; without it, Remaining and Endurance read `—` and a note says so. The block is also
+written into the **CSV** export, as label/value rows under the table.
+
