 ## Tips
 
 - Use the leg inspector for one-off edits, the Plan modal for bulk speed / altitude changes.
-- The Fuel column totals the burn; it does **not** check it against anything. NavAid has no tank-capacity or reserve field and will never warn you that a route exceeds your endurance — compare the total against your own aircraft's usable fuel and your reserve minimum yourself. See [Fuel Calculator](Fuel-Calculator).
+- The **Fuel check** under the table weighs Trip + Reserve + any Alternate against your aircraft's usable fuel and warns in red when the route exceeds what the tanks hold. Set **usable fuel** and **Reserve (min)** on the aircraft for it to check. See [Fuel Calculator](Fuel-Calculator).
 - For long routes that span altitude changes, use **Highlight diff** in the **Chart** menu so you can spot climb / descent legs at a glance on the map while you edit the plan.
 
